<title>USA: Advanced Tissue Sciences FY96 loss narrows.</title>
<headline>Advanced Tissue Sciences FY96 loss narrows.</headline>
<dateline>LA JOLLA, Calif. 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Advanced Tissue Sciences, Inc.</p>
<p>			Consolidated Statement Of Operations</p>
<p>		    (In thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>						  Year Ended December 31,</p>
<p>							   1996	  1995</p>
<p>Revenues:</p>
<p> Product Sales (1)				 $1,018	$1,177</p>
<p> Contracts and fees (2)			  13,574	 2,388</p>
<p> Interest and other				 2,370	 1,185</p>
<p> Total revenues				    16,962	 4,750</p>
<p>Costs and expenses:</p>
<p> Research and development			23,699	18,498</p>
<p> Selling, general and administrative (1)   10,911	 6,115</p>
<p> Professional and consulting		    3,378	 1,897</p>
<p> Cost of goods sold				 1,369	 1,359</p>
<p> Interest						   6	     6</p>
<p> Total costs and expenses			39,363	27,875</p>
<p> Net loss					  (22,401)    (23,125)</p>
<p> Net loss per share				 (.61)	 (.72)</p>
<p> Weighted average shares			 36,556	32,266</p>
<p>(1)  In September 1996, the Company announced its decision to discontinue sales of its Skin(2)(R) laboratory testing kits and took a charge of approximately $1 million associated with the closure of this business.</p>
<p>(2)  In April 1996, the Company signed an agreement to form a joint venture with Smith &amp; Nephew plc for the worldwide commercialization of Dermagraft(R) for the treatment of diabetic foot ulcers.  In connection with the agreement, the Company received a $10 million payment which is included in contracts and fees for the year ended December 31, 1996.</p>
</text>
